MUST-FIX
- "'`src/cli/commands/batch.ts:215` introduces a new executable `batch commands` leaf command, but batch validation still only special-cases `found.name === "batch"` for nested-batch rejection. Repro: `kspec batch --dry-run --commands '"'[{\"command\":\"batch commands\",\"args\":{}}]' --json"'` now returns the generic mutating-only rejection, not the dedicated nested-batch rejection required by `@batch-allowed-commands ac-batch-itself`.
- Please update nested-batch detection in validation to reject any command whose root path is `batch` (e.g. `found.fullPath[1] === "batch"`) before applying the mutating filter.

SHOULD-FIX
- Add a regression test that covers nested `batch commands` in batch input and asserts the same specific nested-batch rejection message, so future subcommands under `batch` cannot silently bypass the specialized error path.

